# LF in the working tree on every platform, Windows included.
#
# Two things here break on CRLF. A shell script with CRLF line endings fails on
# the shebang line before it runs anything, and a fixture with CRLF is not the
# commit message the rule was written against — git writes LF into
# .git/COMMIT_EDITMSG, so a CRLF fixture would test a message no rule ever sees.
* text=auto eol=lf
